-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossacks</a> rise to 40,000 and Crown forces are barred from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kyiv</a>, Bratslav and Chernihiv voivodeships.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1654</span><span class="rf-text">At the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pereiaslav">Pereiaslav</a> Council Khmelnytsky and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossack</a> elite swear allegiance to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsar">Tsar</a> Alexis in return for self-government and war on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1667</span><span class="rf-text">The Treaty of Andrusovo, made without any <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossack</a> representative, splits the Hetmanate along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dnieper">Dnieper</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> and the Commonwealth.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1687</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivan-mazepa">Ivan Mazepa</a> is elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hetman">hetman</a>, ending the civil wars of the Ruin and opening a flowering of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossack</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baroque">Baroque</a> architecture and learning.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1708</span><span class="rf-text">Mazepa allies with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-xii-of-sweden">Charles XII of Sweden</a> on 28 October; on 13 November Menshikov's troops sack Baturyn and kill up to 15,000 people.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1709</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-poltava">Battle of Poltava</a> on 8 July ends in the defeat of the Swedes and Mazepa; the Hetmanate's autonomy becomes nominal.</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1750</span><span class="rf-text